  "(capture_host_oracle.py, 2026-09-12): alphabetical, the first voice default, voiceURI == name, localService true. Every other row is",
  "QUOTED, not measured: which voices a pack carries is Microsoft's 'Appendix A: Supported languages and voices' (Windows 10 and 11 tabs",
  "identical; it spells Hortence, the token is Hortense); the display strings are the OneCore token names as published in the WebbIE",
  "list of Windows 10 voices, kept verbatim with Windows' quirks (Korean (Korean), Catalan (Catalan), Arabic (Saudi), Norwegian (Bokmal),",
  "English (United Kingdom)). gen.voices_keys(platform, locale): the locale's row, else the same language's first row in this order, else en-US.",
  "Sweden's Bengt is not in Appendix A's table but is in the token list; kept."
 ],
